Changes made: the following were extracted from the WN-LMF XML release, and
nothing else is used. Lemmas and forms are lower-cased, lemmas containing a
space are dropped, and every list is sorted by byte order and de-duplicated.

Nouns:
- single-token noun lemmas written in lower case (src/nouns.txt);
- single-token noun lemmas written only with capital letters, kept as known
  words that no rule produces (src/names.txt);
- the noun forms of single-token noun entries, as (form, lemma) pairs,
  unfiltered (FORM_TO_LEMMA and its index LEMMA_TO_PLURAL in src/data.rs).

Other parts of speech:
- single-token lemmas of verbs, of adjectives (adjective satellites included)
  and of adverbs that end in "s", and are in neither the noun nor the name
  list, used only to recognise words WordNet lists as non-nouns (WordNet files
  interjections such as "alas" as adverbs) (src/others.txt);
- the single-token verb, adjective and adverb lemmas written entirely in lower
  case, one list per part of speech (src/verbs.txt, src/adjectives.txt,
  src/adverbs.txt);
- the single-token lemmas of those parts of speech that WordNet writes only
  with capital letters, and not also in lower case in the same part of speech,
  one list per part of speech (src/verb_names.txt, src/adjective_names.txt,
  src/adverb_names.txt);
- the single-token forms of the entries of those lemmas, as (form, lemma)
  pairs, one table per part of speech (VERB_FORMS, ADJECTIVE_FORMS and
  ADVERB_FORMS in src/data.rs), from which the pairs listed in LEMMA_EXCLUDED
  of src/policy.rs are removed.

The hand-written policy lists in src/policy.rs, including LEMMA_CHOICE and
LEMMA_EXCLUDED, are not WordNet data; they are crate source under the
Apache-2.0 licence.

